# Frontend

## neel.js (the shim)
- Plain ES2020, no build step, no dependencies. It is a classic `<script>` only
  (the placeholders make the unrendered file invalid JS, and one file cannot be
  both a classic script and an ES module); module code reads `window.neel`.
- `src/neel/frontend.nim` renders it per request, replacing placeholders with
  JS literals: today `__NEEL_TOKEN__`, `__NEEL_WINDOW_ID__`, `__NEEL_EXPOSED__`;
  serve mode adds `__NEEL_SERVE__`. Each placeholder occurs exactly once, and
  the `static:` block in `frontend.nim` checks the placeholders and the shared
  constants (query parameter names, `/ws` path, the displaced close code)
  against this file. Change both files in the same step.
- The wire format and the public `neel` surface are documented in
  `docs/GUIDE.md` ("The `neel.js` API"): `call` / `ret` / `err` with an optional
  `id`. Keep the shim symmetric with `src/neel/protocol.nim`. `Object.keys(neel)`
  is part of the documented surface; do not add members without updating the
  guide.
- Close codes 1000, 1001, and 4000 (displaced) are final: no reconnect. Any
  other close reconnects with backoff. Treating an unknown code as final or not
  is a protocol decision, never an incidental one: a displaced page that
  reconnects makes two devices displace each other forever.
- Serve-mode-only behavior (the dormant state and wake-up reconnects) is gated
  on the rendered serve flag; local mode behavior stays exactly as documented.
- Reject with an `Error` whose `name` is the Nim exception kind and `message` is
  the Nim message, so `catch (e) { e.name === "ValueError" }` works.

## Examples
- Use absolute asset paths (`/main.js`, `/style.css`); the server serves the
  web folder at `/`.
- Never assign untrusted strings to `innerHTML`; use `textContent`.
- Prefer self-contained assets over CDN links so release builds embed
  everything.
- Serve-mode examples request their initial state with a `neel.<name>()` call
  on load and never act on URL parameters without user confirmation.

```js
// good
const name = await neel.filePicker(dir);
out.textContent = name;

// fire-and-forget
neel.log.send("clicked");
```
